  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n\nThe central idea is to use adaptive wavelet-based optimization to refine the parent solution. This requires transitioning from piecewise constant functions (0/1) to continuous functions for smoother optimization landscapes, while explicitly incorporating the boundary constraints and maintaining the sum constraint. \n\nWe target a solution that shows periodic properties, as autapses in relevant literature suggest near-optimal solutions exhibit periodic wave patterns. The approach will involve:\n\n- Using wavelet den sification to explore finer-scale features\n- Employing gradient-based optimization with careful constraint handling\n- Expanding the search to larger resolutions while using the parent solution as a base\n- Implementing multi-resolution optimization with a fallback to the parent solution if needed\n\nThe method addresses the limitations of the provided approach by:\n- Providing explicit guarantees for the solution bounds\n- Enforcing the constraints through careful projection\n- Allowing upscaling to higher resolutions for better approximation\n- Incorporating both binary and continuous representations of the solution\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n\nDefine:\n- Objective: Minimize C = max_k \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n- Constraints:\n  - 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 for all x\n  - \u222b h(x)dx = 1\n  - Define domain [0,2] with dx = 2/N for N samples\n\nFor optimization:\n- Represent h as a piecewise linear function on N points\n- Use the following formulation for optimization:\n  $\\underset{h}{\\min} \\max_{-(n-1) \\leq k \\leq n-1} \\left( \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} h_i (1 - h_{i+k}) \\right) \\times \\frac{\\text{PCF}}{4}$\n- Where PCF is the pairwise correlation factor applied to stabilize the optimization\n- Use CVXPY to model the convex relaxation of the problem\n- Project solutions to the feasible set using damped iterations\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n\nPhase 1: Initialization\n- Use parent solution scaled to target resolution if N > 960\n- For N \u2264 960, generate a candidate by:\n  * Downsampling parent (keeping proportional values)\n  * Adding small perturbations\n  * Projecting to satisfy the sum constraint\n\nPhase 2: Multi-resolution search\n- Use wavelet decomposition of the initial candidate\n- Decompose into approximation and detail coefficients\n- Insert 3 scales of detail coefficients to maintain periodic properties\n- Optimize each resolution level separately with damped projection\n\nPhase 3: Optimization loop\n  - For each resolution:\n    * Use CVXPY to optimize with:\n        Minimize: (scaled) max_k correlation\n        Subject to:\n          (1) h_i in [0, 1] for all i\n          (2) Sum_{i} h_i = N/2 (approximately original sum)\n          (3) Auto-pairing constraints (from parent solution structure)\n\n  - Optimization uses penalization method to enforce all constraints\n  - Project solutions using damping and coordinate normalization\n\nPhase 4: Fall-back mechanism\n- If at any resolution the CMPSEA exceeds the original record, revert to wavelet denoised version\n- Use a temporal monitoring of objective to decide continuation\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations:\n\nDefault configuration:\n- Start with resolution = 1250 (optimization from parent)\n- Number of iterations: 15 at each scale (adaptive if objective plateaus)\n- Wavelet kernel: Db4 with 3 vanishing moments\n- Temperature schedule for GLPK/MOSEK: decrease from 2000 to 50 over iterations\n\nVarying strategies:\n- Tuesday\u30b5\u30f3\u30c9\u30a4\u30c3\u30c1):\n  * When stuck, perturb the wavelets and restart optimization\n-Phase-specific scale adjustment:\n  * Detail coefficients always use a minimum scale factor to maintain periodicity\n-Windowed objective function:\n  * When long-range correlations dominate, restrict shift k to approximately \u00b14 samples\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness:\n\nEstimated time allocation:\n- Resolution scaling: ~10s\n- Wavelet processing: ~150s\n- Optimization loop: ~500s (with adaptive exit conditions)\n- Fall-back: if objective too high, revert to previous best\n-Overall parallelization: each resolution level runs concurrently\n\nImplementation ensures:\n- Stability with damped projection onto L1 unit sphere\n- Feasibility check at each step:\n  - Sum constraint \u00b11e-5\n  - All values within [0,1]\n- Pre-definition of wavelet basis\n\nTermination conditions:\n- Satisfactory improvement over parent (at least 0.98%)\n- Local optimization plateau (no change of 0.005% for 3 iterations)\n- Exceeded 1300s\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\n\nFinal validation includes:\n- Check all correlations for \u2248200 shifts (not just full set)\n- Ensure finite values for all metrics\n- Re-evaluate using:\n  $\\text{target} = (\\max_k \\sum_i h_i (1-h_{i+k}) \\times (2/len(h)))$\n- Small checks done for different resolution levels\n\nRepresentation must satisfy:\n- h[i] \u2208 [0,1] with tolerance 1e-6\n- \u2211h[i] \u2248 N/2 within 1e-4\n- Correlation computation uses full mode with appropriate scaling\n\nOutput format:\n- (h_array, c5_value, num_points)\n- All arrays must be real-valued, not block-decomposed",
